# No .gitattributes existed before, so a Windows checkout's default
# core.autocrlf converts every text file to CRLF on the way out of git —
# which then floods `eslint --cache .`'s prettier/prettier rule with a
# "Delete `␍`" warning per line across dozens of files it never cached
# before, on windows-latest CI specifically. That's at minimum a lot of
# needless noise, and turned up alongside two reproducible hangs in the
# Lint step on this same runner, so line endings are pinned here rather
# than left to whatever the checkout machine's global git config happens
# to default to.
* text=auto eol=lf
